findings.claim:
Test 9 still refuses recoveries made by definitions alone whenever a package definition reached at a term position holds a package proof that carries no fact into the recovery:
- a termination proof by a package lemma;
- a package instance of a Prop class passed to a model definition;
- a model relation built on a root definition that holds a root proof (test 9, unlike the bridges' closed set, does not exempt admitted theorems).

This follows test 9's mechanism bullets, but it contradicts the condition's headline ('by definitions alone'). §3.2's 'What this does not show' lists only the opposite case. Its termination control covers only `decreasing_by omega`, so §9's REGRESSIONS-1 row reads as if termination proofs were handled in general.
